{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Say.</b> Like זָכוֹר, שָׁמוֹר — דישנ\"ט בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>Say to them.</b> So that all of them hear (ibid.)." "<b>Say.</b> Full spelling — do not bless them in haste and agitation, but with intention and a whole heart (Tanchuma)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French destindrent, a plural imperative form meaning 'stop' or 'pause'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:42.796959774Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}